+## Build
 
-See [blender.org/about/license](https://www.blender.org/about/license) for details.
+Follow the official [Blender platform build instructions](https://developer.blender.org/docs/handbook/building_blender/), install Rust 1.88 or newer, then configure with the Redrob Shape profile:
+
+```sh
+cmake -S . -B ../build_shape \
+  -C build_files/cmake/config/redrob_shape.cmake
+cmake --build ../build_shape --config Release
+```
+
+A normal Blender configure remains unchanged and does not require Rust; `WITH_REDROB_AGENT` defaults to `OFF` unless the Redrob Shape profile is selected.
+
+## Connect Redrob
+
+Create or approve a workspace key in [Redrob Console](https://console.redrob.ai/guide), then launch Blender with:
+
+```sh
+export REDROB_API_KEY="your-workspace-key"
+```
+
+The default API route is `https://console.redrob.ai/api/backend/v1/chat/completions` with model `auto`. The sidecar reads the key from its environment; the key is not sent over the Blender protocol, stored in `.blend` data, or written to logs.
+
+[Redrob Code](https://console.redrob.ai/code) can be used independently for repository development and upstream modernization. It is not a runtime dependency of Redrob Shape.
+
+## Blender compatibility and upstream
+
+The Blender executable names, CMake targets, file-format versions, platform application IDs, operators, keymaps, and startup precedence are intentionally retained. See [UPSTREAM.md](UPSTREAM.md) for the exact baseline and sync policy.
+
+General Blender fixes should follow [Blender's official contribution process](https://developer.blender.org/docs/handbook/contributing/). Redrob Shape contributions should follow [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md).
+
